WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.270
All right, it's time for Drew's News,

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.690
your comfy, oversized, good news sweater.

3
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.170
And with me at the desk, my main thread, Ross Mathews.

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.010
Yes, hi everybody. (crowd cheers and claps)

5
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.652
Hi. Hi Drew.

6
00:00:12.652 --> 00:00:16.340
(crowd cheers and claps) (Ross laughs)

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.320
I love this outfit.

8
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.580
Yeah, I took a risk today.

9
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.767
Pattern on pattern, but it's Design Week, hello.

10
00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.580
It's giving me all the feels and we're both in vests.

11
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.190
Yeah, we are vest dressed.

12
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.023
We are vest dressed.

13
00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:29.507
Yeah, and I am invested in our looks today. (laughs)

14
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:31.380
Oh, invested, come on.

15
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.760
Come on, I know.

16
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.730
God, that was good.

17
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.110
You are the king of puns

18
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.533
and you just warm the cockles of my heart when you do it.

19
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.550
Oh, thanks. (crowd laughs)

20
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.860
And I'm really excited because beyond Design Week,

21
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.390
it is International Women's Day.

22
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.343
Yeah. (crowd cheers and claps) Yes.

23
00:00:48.343 --> 00:00:50.730
Today is the day to celebrate women

24
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.760
all around the world that have achieved

25
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.130
that often totally against the odds, you know, accolades.

26
00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.400
And it's also a day to focus on

27
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.480
how we can break down all the biases around us

28
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.840
and even get closer to gender equality.

29
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.510
And People magazine is doing just that,

30
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.030
celebrating with their special

31
00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.830
Women Changing the World issue.

32
00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.891
Check out our cover girl, Lizzo.

33
00:01:12.891 --> 00:01:13.954
Yes, Lizzo. (crowd cheers and claps)

34
00:01:13.954 --> 00:01:18.121
Because before Lizzo, there was no Lizzo.

35
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:19.980 line:15%
That's true.

36
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.440 line:15%
The Grammy winning rapper, singer, actor

37
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.300 line:15%
and total charm machine says she blazed her own path

38
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.010 line:15%
with one goal in mind, showing the world

39
00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.430 line:15%
that this is what success can look like.

40
00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:33.420 line:15%
And she wants to embrace and empower

41
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.280 line:15%
women all over the world who identify with her,

42
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.890 line:15%
who might not think they fit in the mold

43
00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.090 line:15%
and she's gonna blast right through that mold.

44
00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:41.923 line:15%
Yes, she is.

45
00:01:41.923 --> 00:01:42.810 line:15%
This is so awesome.

46
00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.360 line:15%
It's so awesome, and Lizzo just proves

47
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.370 line:15%
that if you don't fit the mold,

48
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.270 line:15%
then break the mold, make your own mold, right.

49
00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.610 line:15%
Right? Yes. (crowd cheers and claps)

50
00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.727 line:15%
And so many women do that, you know,

51
00:01:51.727 --> 00:01:54.770 line:15%
and this issue celebrates game changers across every field

52
00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.220 line:15%
like Emily Penn who's an ocean activist

53
00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.340 line:15%
who started Expedition, an all women sailing

54
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.900
research team that fights ocean pollution

55
00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.180
and Monica Johnson in Louisiana.

56
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.870
Her nonprofit, Heroes, offers medical care,

57
00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.940
counseling and professional training

58
00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.410
to HIV positive members of her community.

59
00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.700
So, there are women all over this country

60
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.533
making such a difference.

61
00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:17.366
(crowd claps)

62
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:19.020
I'm such a People magazine fan.

63
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.610
I subscribe to it, I get it every week.

64
00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.443
Mm-hmm.

65
00:02:22.443 --> 00:02:24.650
And I wanna thank them for for shining the spotlight

66
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.000
on these amazing women

67
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.920
'cause this issue is on news stands now.

68
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.710
And it actually leads me to a pick

69
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.490
from "Drew's Little Yellow Book",

70
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.470
which is my personal curation.

71
00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.069
(crowd cheers and claps)

72
00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:39.373
But this is something very personal to me.

73
00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:43.300
This is "Good Night Stories for Rebel Girls",

74
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.570
and I'm reading this with my daughters right now.

75
00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.660
There's actually two volumes

76
00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.600
and they're just great historical confirmations

77
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.206
that there's nothing women can't do.

78
00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.661
Hey, how about that.

79
00:02:55.661 --> 00:02:58.828 line:15%
(upbeat theme music)

